THE VALUES
The existing footer is bg-[#f5f3f3] with border-t border-[#c6c6cc]/20 (app/page.tsx:660).
#f5f3f3 converts to oklch(0.966 0.002 17.2) — only 0.018 below paper, because the
separation is carried by the hairline top border rather than by the fill.

Dark follows the same rule the other bands do, mirroring the offset rather than the
colour: 0.018 BELOW paper in light becomes 0.018 ABOVE it in dark, so 0.181.

  band            light L   dark L   delta vs base
  paper (base)      0.984    0.163   —
  warm              0.935    0.212   -0.049 -> +0.049
  slab              0.134    0.268   -0.850 -> +0.105
  footer            0.966    0.181   -0.018 -> +0.018

CONSEQUENCE FOR THE TOKENS
The footer is now light in light theme and dark in dark theme, exactly like paper, so it
takes the paper-ground text tokens (fg, muted, brass-text). The *-on-slab set narrows to
serving the slab alone, which is better-named than it was: those tokens now describe
precisely one band.

A SECOND DEFECT THIS SURFACED
Raising the dark footer to 0.181 pushed the hairline rule against it to 1.38:1, under the
1.4:1 floor this project uses for decorative rules. --landing-hairline lifts 0.300 -> 0.325
in dark, which clears the footer at 1.51:1 and improves the rule on paper from 1.42:1 to
1.55:1. Light theme unaffected.

DESIGN NOTE
This leaves the 'Why it matters' slab as the page's only dark band. That sharpens it rather
than weakening the composition — the drama is no longer repeated at the bottom of the page.

